              <p>Figma, Illustrator, Photoshop, Canva, wireframing.</p>
            </article>
            <article className="capability-card">
              <h3>Languages</h3>
              <p>C, Java, Python, JavaScript, SQL.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="studio-section" id="craft">
          <div className="studio-section__header">
            <p className="studio-section__eyebrow">Deep dives into our craft</p>
            <h2>Experience, events, and design thinking.</h2>
            <p>
              These cards replace the older component layout with a tighter, more case-study-like story flow.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div className="craft-grid">
            {craftCards.map((card) => (
              <article className="craft-card" key={card.number}>
                <div className="craft-card__number">{card.number}</div>
                <div className="craft-card__content">
                  <p className="craft-card__subtitle">{card.subtitle}</p>
                  <h3>{card.title}</h3>
                  <p>{card.body}</p>
                  <ul>
                    {card.list.map((item) => (
                      <li key={item}>{item}</li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div className="event-marquee" aria-label="events attended">
            {events.map((event) => (
              <span key={event}>{event}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="studio-section" id="recognition">
          <div className="studio-section__header">
            <p className="studio-section__eyebrow">Recognition</p>
            <h2>Certificates and measured output.</h2>
            <p>
              The certificates and project count become a more prominent visual system here, similar to the award and stat blocks in the reference.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div className="recognition-grid">
            <div className="recognition-stats">
              <article className="recognition-stat">
                <span>19 years</span>
                <p>Portfolio timeline style data point, kept as a high-visibility stat from the original references to studio credibility.</p>
              </article>
              <article className="recognition-stat">
                <span>6 projects</span>
                <p>Cleanly represented as selected work instead of scattered cards.</p>
              </article>
              <article className="recognition-stat">
                <span>3 certificates</span>
                <p>MongoDB, Oracle APEX, and Java Foundation remain accessible as proof points.</p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div className="recognition-cards">
              {recognitionCards.map((item) => (
                <article className="recognition-card" key={item.title}>
                  <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                  <p>{item.body}</p>
                  <a href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                    View certificate
                  </a>
                </article>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="studio-section studio-contact" id="contact">
          <div className="studio-section__header">
            <p className="studio-section__eyebrow">Contact</p>
            <h2>Let’s build the next version.</h2>
            <p>
              Keep the same career data, but present it with a cleaner and more premium visual system.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div className="contact-grid">
            <article className="contact-card">
              <span>WhatsApp</span>
              <strong>6384248520</strong>
              <p>Response within 24 hours</p>
            </article>
            <article className="contact-card contact-card--link" onClick={() => window.open("https://www.linkedin.com/in/dhanush-s-679674337/", "_blank")} role="button" tabIndex={0}>
              <span>LinkedIn</span>
              <strong>linkedin.com/in/dhanush-s-679674337</strong>
              <p>Professional connection</p>
            </article>
            <article className="contact-card">
              <span>GitHub</span>
              <strong>github.com/dhanush1009</strong>
              <p>Browse recent builds</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div className="contact-cta">
            <button className="studio-button studio-button--primary" onClick={() => scrollInto("home")}>Back to top</button>
            <button className="studio-button studio-button--ghost" onClick={() => scrollInto("work")}>Review work again</button>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer className="studio-footer">
        <p>Dhanush Studio · React portfolio rebuilt with a darker editorial layout.</p>
        <div className="studio-footer__links">
          <button onClick={() => scrollInto("work")}>Projects</button>
          <button onClick={() => scrollInto("craft")}>Experience</button>
          <button onClick={() => scrollInto("contact")}>Contact</button>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  );
